# {{instance_name}}-site

Hugo site for **{{instance_name}}**. Scaffolded by kestrel's
`/instantiate-site` meta-skill (ROADMAP/KITS.md §3/§5) from
`library/scaffolds/site/`.

## Content-writer contract

Registry/attention-derived content is written ONLY by the kestrel publish
core, through this instance's own adapter (the single-content-writer
invariant, ROADMAP/DESIGN.md §1: "A site repo has exactly one content
writer: the publish core, through that site's adapter"). Once that adapter
exists (see `/instantiate-site`'s adapter-stub step), do not hand-edit
whatever paths it owns — those belong upstream, in the data repo or the
adapter.

Editorial chrome — `layouts/`, `static/css/`, and any hand-authored
editorial pages you add under `content/` — is normal repo-owned code,
edited directly. The invariant governs generated content only, never the
site chrome.

## Fonts

None are bundled here. Fonts are a brand asset, chosen per-site once this
instance has a real design system — self-hosting under `static/fonts/` is
a proven pattern elsewhere in this fleet, but it is not a default to
inherit sight-unseen; pick fonts deliberately, later.

## Build & deploy

- Local: `hugo --minify` (targets Hugo 0.111.3-extended; no theme
  dependencies, no Hugo modules, no external assets referenced at build
  time).
- Cloudflare: build command `hugo`, output directory `public`, with
  `HUGO_VERSION` pinned to match. `static/_headers` carries baseline
  security headers; `enableRobotsTXT` is on in `hugo.yaml`.
- Before this repo builds for real: set a real `baseURL` in `hugo.yaml`
  (currently a placeholder), and give it a real Cloudflare Pages/Workers
  project `name` in `wrangler.toml` if that should differ from
  `{{instance_name}}`. Both are Ben's calls, not this scaffold's.

## Next steps

1. Choose this instance's brand palette and type system, and fill in the
   commented custom properties in `static/css/main.css`.
2. Write this instance's own `publish/adapter.py` **in the sibling data
   repo** (declared via that repo's `kestrel.yaml` `outputs.adapter` —
   adapters are instance-owned, not engine code) — the `/instantiate-site`
   skill sketches its shape (module docstring, `ROOT`/env resolution,
   empty build hooks); it ships as a `NotImplementedError` stub, not
   working code, at this phase.
3. Register this site as some data instance's `site:` sibling in
   kestrel's own `instances.yaml`, then run `/install-kit` against it to
   bring in this site's agent docs.
